## THE DECISIONS INSIDE THIS LANE (each Tuesday's default as coordinator; each a Question at the stamp; each a behaviour with a cell)
- **D1 THE LIBRARY AND ITS REFERENCES** (Q1). `Datasec.Suite.Identity` references `Datasec.Suite.Graph` only (which brings `Datasec.Suite.Logging` and its two packages, already in the cache: the lock rule). It does NOT implement lane A1's `ICardIdentityService` and does not reference `Datasec.Suite.SignIn` (lane F1 owns that folder tonight; the adapter that maps a `CardLookupResult` to the sign-in actor's `CardUser` is a later lane's). Cell L02.
- **D2 THE NAMES AND LIMITS** (Q2). `CsaLimits`: `AttributeSet` = `HPAuthenticationSuite`, `CardAttribute` = `cardId`, `CardsPerUser` = 15, `ValuesPerUser` = 50, `PrefixLength` = 62, `BlobLength` = 64, none configurable (pointers 7 to 9, 14, 16). Cells E01, E04, E05, F01.
- **D3 THE BLOB MAKER IS HANDED IN** (Q3). `ICardBlobCodec` (`SearchPrefix(cardId)`, `Blob(cardId, mail)`): the store never holds a key. What it is handed is checked before use: a prefix of exactly 62 and a blob of exactly 64 characters, each from the base64url alphabet, the blob starting with the prefix; a maker that throws or answers otherwise is `CodecFailed` and the prefix never reaches a request (so no quote or space can enter the search filter). Cell F08.
- **D4 THE SEARCH** (Q4, STOP-CLASS: S4 answers it in words). ONE `GET users?$count=true&$select=id,userPrincipalName,displayName,givenName,surname,mail,customSecurityAttributes&$filter=customSecurityAttributes/HPAuthenticationSuite/cardId/any(c:startswith(c,'<prefix>'))` with the header `ConsistencyLevel: eventual` (pointer 10, the Workpath app's call). Then, per answered user, the whole blob is made for THAT user's mail (for no mail when the user has none) and compared ordinally with the user's entries. **Two rules differ from the Workpath app on purpose:** a failed status of the search is `CsaStoreException(GraphFailed)`, never "no user" (pointer 13 sends an existing user down the enrolment path); an answer with `@odata.nextLink` is `Ambiguous` and nobody is chosen (pointer 12 reads the first page as if it were all). Cells F01, F04, F06, F11.
- **D5 THE FOUR OUTCOMES** (Q5). `Found` (exactly one user holds the whole blob; the user is returned), `NotFound` (nobody holds the prefix), `AssociationInvalid` (users hold the prefix, none the whole blob for their own mail: the Workpath app's "Card-user association is invalid.", pointer 10's line), `Ambiguous` (two or more holders, or a next page). A user whose collection holds the blob twice is found once. Cells F01 to F05.
- **D6 THE READ AND THE COUNT RULE** (Q6). `ReadAttributesAsync(objectId)`: ONE `GET users/<id>?$select=id,mail,customSecurityAttributes`; the answer's `id` must be the asked identifier. Each single value (string, number, boolean) counts one, each collection entry one, names holding `@` (annotations) none; the card entries come back in the answer's order, duplicates kept; any other shape (an object value, a non-string card, a name twice, the set not an object) is `MalformedAnswer` and nothing is used. A user with no attributes, or a null set, reads empty. An attribute name the schema does not hold is counted like any other. Cells R01 to R04, F07.
- **D7 THE ENROLMENT** (Q7). The schema check (D8); the search (D4) must answer no OTHER user holding the prefix, and no next page, else `HeldByAnotherUser` and nothing more is read or written; the user's read (D6), whose mail makes the blob; the blob already held: `AlreadyEnrolled`; 15 or more entries: `CardLimitReached`; one more value past 50: `ValueLimitReached`; else ONE `PATCH users/<id>` of the whole card collection (the held entries in their order, the new blob at the end), with the two `@odata.type` annotations and NO other attribute: `Enrolled`. Entries are counted as held, so an entry held twice counts twice. A user whose mail changed keeps the old entry and gains a new one; both count (a named limit). Cells E01 to E10.
- **D8 THE SCHEMA CHECK, NEVER THE CREATION** (Q8, STOP-CLASS: S4 answers it in words). `EnsureSchemaAsync`: `GET directory/attributeSets/HPAuthenticationSuite` (its `id` must be the set's name), then `GET directory/customSecurityAttributeDefinitions/HPAuthenticationSuite_cardId` (its `type` the string `String`, `isCollection` true, `isSearchable` true, each as JSON of that kind); a 404 on either is `SchemaMissing`, another definition `SchemaMismatch`. A passed check is kept for `SchemaCacheLifetime` (default 1 hour; 1 second to 24 hours) on the store's `TimeProvider`; a failed check is not kept. Only `EnrolCardAsync` runs it; the search and the read do not. **The store never creates the set or the definition.** Cells K01 to K05.
- **D9 THE ARGUMENTS** (Q9). A card follows the card rule of lane A1 (1 to 32 characters, each from space to tilde, not blank, no upper-case letter), else `ArgumentException` before any request; an object id must parse as an identifier and is sent in its lower-case hyphen form (so braces and upper case reach the same user). Cells F09, F10, R04, R05, E09.
- **D10 ONLY TYPED RESULTS LEAVE; NO VALUE IN A TEXT** (Q10). Every call returns its typed result, or throws `ArgumentNullException` / `ArgumentException` before any request, `CsaStoreException` (`GraphFailed` with the Graph layer's exception inside, `MalformedAnswer`, `CodecFailed`, `SchemaMissing`, `SchemaMismatch`) after which nothing of that call is used or written, or the caller's cancellation as the Graph layer raises it. `CsaUser`, `CardLookupResult`, `CsaAttributes` and the exception messages print fixed masks or counts. Cells L01, L03, L04, F06, F07, E08, R06.
- **D11 NO LOGGING, NO NETWORK OF ITS OWN, NO TIMER, NO WRITABLE STATIC** (Q10). Requests only through `GraphClient.SendAsync`; time only through the store's `TimeProvider`; ONE `HttpMethod.Patch` in the library and no POST, PUT or DELETE. Cell L02 and `boundary.py`.
- **D12 A CANCELLED CALL** (Q10). The caller's cancellation passes through untyped (`OperationCanceledException` or a subclass) and nothing is written. Cell L04.
- **D13 THE PROTOTYPE IS HANDED OVER AS FROZEN PATCHES** (Q13). The drafter's prototype (the first drafter's code, reviewed, corrected and extended by this drafter: the report says what) is `1-red.diff` plus `2-fix.diff`; you apply them byte for byte and write no product or test line of your own. Alternative: the seat writes its own from THE CONTRACT (two implementations for the gate; about 2000 lines; kit B1914 gave the sign-in lane's seat 240 minutes for that size).
- **D14 THE CONTRACT'S NAMES** (Q14): THE CONTRACT below.

## THE CONTRACT (by PROPERTY first; the patches hold it; the names are DEFAULTS of Q14)
**The property.** The store maps a card to at most one user only when exactly one answered user holds the card's whole blob for that user's own mail on a single-page answer; it writes a user's card collection only by ONE PATCH that keeps every held entry in order and adds one blob, and only under both limits, the schema check passed and no other user holding the card's prefix; nothing it is handed out of form reaches a request; no text it makes holds a card, a blob, a user, a mail, a name or a token. **Parts, namespace `Datasec.Suite.Identity`, files under `src/Datasec.Suite.Identity/` (MEASURED: `2-fix.diff` applied; any other shape: STOP):** `CsaStore` (sealed: `CsaStore(GraphClient graph, IGraphTokenSource appTokens, ICardBlobCodec codec, CsaOptions options, TimeProvider? time = null)`, `FindUserByCardAsync`, `ReadAttributesAsync`, `EnrolCardAsync`, `EnsureSchemaAsync`; `CsaStore.cs:37`, `:61`, `:92`, `:106`, `:154`); `ICardBlobCodec`; `CsaOptions` (`SchemaCacheLifetime`); `CsaLimits`; `CardLookupOutcome`, `CardLookupResult` (constructor `internal`), `EnrolOutcome`; `CsaUser` (constructor `internal`); `CsaAttributes` (constructor `internal`; `CardIds`, `ValueCount`, `TryGetString`); `CsaFailure`, `CsaStoreException` (constructor `internal`); `internal static class CsaReading`; `README.md` (for engineers, with a `## Limits` section).

## THE REQUIRED SECTION: what is the store handed that is NOT the tested shape?
**The property: whatever a caller, the blob maker, the Graph layer or the tenant's answers hand the store, each call ends in its typed result or one of the exceptions of D10, never another exception and never a user chosen or a collection written outside the property of THE CONTRACT.** At least these, each with its cell (MEASURED green on `<d>/clone3`, red against the stubs); any other shape you meet: give it a cell or name it as a limit in STATUS, never leave it out.
